			"Message": "build(Echo): Re-enable suppressed warnings in build script for development\n\nRestore `#![allow]` attributes in `build.rs` to cover `non_snake_case`, `non_camel_case_types`, `non_upper_case_globals`, `dead_code`, `unused_imports`, `unused_variables`, and `unused_assignments`. This aligns the build script's linting tolerance with recent updates to `Source/Library.rs`, ensuring a warning-free build during active refactoring of the work-stealing scheduler.\n\nThe previous removal of these allowances has been reverted to maintain consistency across the codebase and prevent CI/build failures due to generated code warnings.",
			"SHA": "f7a24af8f7e7b958633017549fb0179a3bd10393"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T04:20:33Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				57,
				3
			],
			"Message": "build(Echo): Update devDependencies and suppress unused code warnings\n\nBump Cloudflare Workers toolchain to the latest versions: @cloudflare/workers-types to 4.20260523.1, miniflare to 4.20260521.0, and wrangler to 4.94.0. This keeps the local testing environment aligned with the latest upstream changes.\n\nAdditionally, expand the `#![allow]` attributes in `Source/Library.rs` to include `dead_code`, `unused_imports`, `unused_variables`, and `unused_assignments` for the Rust core. These attributes are added to suppress build warnings arising from active refactoring within the work-stealing scheduler implementation. The `non_snake_case` allowance is removed from `build.rs` as it is no longer required.\n\nThis update ensures a clean build during development phases and maintains the stability of the local Wrangler testing infrastructure.",
			"SHA": "7e1de9b9741eb7d5f7dd60ec9b157e96826a004f"
		},
